<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 313 0 R
/E (Libraries have evolved significantly, from manual record-keeping to digital systems that enhance efficiency and accessibility. Traditional methods often led to misplaced books, duplicate records, and delayed updates. The Department Library Management System modernizes these operations by automating tasks such as book issuance, returns, inventory management, and user registration. By digitizing records, it reduces manual errors, improves resource tracking, and optimizes library workflows.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
158 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 314 0 R
/E (This system not only enhances efficiency but also improves the user experience for students, faculty, and library staff. With features like real-time book availability, advanced search options, and automated fine management, it ensures seamless access to resources. The intuitive interface makes it easy to navigate, promoting a well-organized, accessible, and technology-driven library environment.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [2]
>>
