/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 321 0 R
/E (Library Management Systems \(LMS\) face issues like complex interfaces, poor search functionality, scalability limits, and security risks. Many lack integration with other tools, mobile accessibility, and automation for routine tasks, adding to staff workload. High upgrade costs, inadequate backups, and licensing restrictions create financial and operational hurdles. Addressing these challenges is key to ensuring an efficient, secure, and user-friendly system.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
